{"id":"000VZX","title":"Oh, these date formats 20-01-08 Sudoku","author":"Dashiel","solvedCount":0,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-11T15:20:29+00:00","posted":"Heute, 16:01 Uhr","rules":"Solve in SudokuPad\n\nNormal sudoku rules: each digit 1–9 appears once in every row, column and 3×3 box.\n\nGerman whisper lines (green): Adjacent digits along a line differ by at least 5.\n\nKiller cages: Digits in a dashed cage sum to the number in its corner and may not repeat within the cage.\n\nBlack Kropki dots: One digit is exactly double the other. Not all possible dots are given.\n\nDate line (pink, wide): Each pink line consists of exactly 6 cells and represents the date given above in DDMMYY format. The order of the three date parts and the reading direction of the line are unknown, but all three parts must be read in the same direction. For example, 2-0-0-1-0-8 can be 20-01-08, 08-01-20 or 20-08-01, but not 20-01-80, because the year digits would then be read in the opposite direction.\n\nZeros on date lines: A 0 is not a digit and is not entered in the grid. Instead, each 0 stands for an unknown digit that is entered in the sudoku as usual. Every 0 must take its own value, different from all other 0 jokers across all date lines.","solutionCode":"Digits of row 5, left to right","tags":["Sudoku","Kropki Pairs (Variante)","Killer (Variante)","German Whispers (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/ozun009pnx","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/ozun009pnx","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":3,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-11T15:20:29+00:00"}